{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0043","billNumberShort":"H.B. 43","billNumberLong":"HB0043S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0065","shortTitle":"School Security Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"WILCORD","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Wilcox, Ryan D.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"","floorSponsorName":"","floorSponsorHouse":"","generalProvisions":"This bill creates the School Safety Support Program to provide funding for school safety requirements and infrastructure.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>creates the School Safety Support Program (program) to fund school safety personnel, building standards, emergency protocols, and security infrastructure;<hr><ltbullet>establishes a distribution formula that allocates funding to charter schools and school districts based on enrollment and base amounts;<hr><ltbullet>requires local education agencies to submit safety plans and annual reports to receive funding;<hr><ltbullet>adds the program to the list of education programs eligible for annual inflation and enrollment growth adjustments;<hr><ltbullet>protects the program from funding reductions due to negative enrollment growth;<hr><ltbullet>directs the state board to collaborate with the School Safety Center and state security chief to establish rules and monitor implementation; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Jeff Van Hulten","fiscalAnalyst":"Rachelle Gunderson","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"BDFDLIJUOW","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2025-12-18 20:58:07.690","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","o